<title>UK: Landell Mills sees 96/97 cocoa deficit at 150,000T.</title>
<headline>Landell Mills sees 96/97 cocoa deficit at 150,000T.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The world cocoa deficit is forecast at 150,000 tonnes in 1996/97 (Oct-Sept) against an estimated surplus of 100,000 tonnes in 1995/96, UK research house Landell Mills Commodities (LMC) said. An LMC official however declined further details. LMC had earlier put the 1995/96 cocoa surplus at 65,000 tonnes.</p>
<p>The International Cocoa Organization (ICCO) on Monday put the 1996/97 deficit at 225,000 tonnes and 1995/96 surplus at 120,000. -- London newsroom +44 171 542 4985</p>
